given-names></name><name><surname>Getz</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hargrove</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>de Zoysa</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Dye</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Auvert</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The potential impact of male circumcision on HIV in sub-Saharan Africa</article-title><source>PLos Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>e262</fpage><comment>Published online 2006 July 11. doi: 10.1371/journal.pmed.0030262.</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16822094</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pmed.0030262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Viljoen</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The acceptability of male circumcision as an HIV intervention among a rural Zulu population, KwaZulu, Natal, South Africa</article-title><source>AIDS Care</source><year>2005</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15832878</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/09540120412331299744</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ngalande</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapondo</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acceptability of male circumcision for the prevention of HIV infection in Malawi</article-title><source>AIDS Behav</source><year>2006</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>85